<title>USA: Fidelity Investments equity head seen leaving - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Fidelity Investments equity head seen leaving - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Investments' Bart Grenier, assistant head of the firm's equity division, is thinking of leaving the company to work for DDJ Capital Management in Boston, the Wall Street Journal said in its electronic edition on Monday.</p>
<p>According to people close to the matter, Grenier, 38, could announce his decision as early as today, the paper said.</p>
<p>DDJ Capital trades distressed securities, it said.</p>
<p>Grenier was quoted as declining to comment.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
